-- Regression: compiled `to_string` printed `#<tag:N>` for any type DECLARED
-- inside a module but DENOTED by its bare short name.
--
-- A `ptype` in `mod File` lowers to the TIR name `File.FileError`, but every
-- annotation and builtin signature denotes it bare, so the value reaching a
-- render site has static type `FileError`. `Llvm_ctor_desc.id_for` looked the
-- descriptor up by EXACT name, missed, and fell through to the untyped
-- renderer -- while the interpreter, which keeps the declaration, printed the
-- constructor. `file_read` on a missing path is the case a user actually hits.
--
-- This is the same bare-vs-qualified split `Llvm_data.ctor_entry` already
-- resolved for CONSTRUCTOR keys by suffix search; type names needed it too.
-- `assign_ids` now also registers each qualified name's short name as an
-- alias for the same descriptor id.
--
-- Note what this is NOT: the error cell here is built by the C runtime
-- (`mk_file_error`, runtime/march_runtime.c), so its header carries no type
-- id. It renders correctly anyway, because the STATIC path walks the
-- descriptor by tag and never consults the header. Stamping the C builders is
-- a separate, still-open item.
--
-- The `dup_` lines pin the deliberately CONSERVATIVE half: a short name
-- declared by two modules is ambiguous, so no alias is registered and the
-- value keeps the placeholder it has always had. Two control runs with the
-- ambiguity guard removed showed it prevents no wrong name on its own
-- (colliding types get globally-unique tags, which cannot match a C-built
-- cell's declaration-order tag, and a stamped cell is corrected by its own
-- header id) -- the guard is kept so that correctness does not RELY on either
-- of those, and its cost is only that these two lines stay placeholders.
-- Asserted as a boolean, not exact text: the placeholder embeds a global tag
-- number that any unrelated tag renumbering would shift.

mod QualifiedTypeNameRender do
  needs IO.Console
  needs IO.FileRead

  fn main(_c : Cap(IO.Console), _f : Cap(IO.FileRead)) : Unit do
    match file_read("/definitely/missing/path.txt") do
    Ok(_)  -> println("file=ok")
    Err(e) -> println("file_err=" ++ to_string(e))
    end

    match dir_list("/definitely/missing/dir") do
    Ok(_)  -> println("dir=ok")
    Err(e) -> println("dir_err=" ++ to_string(e))
    end

    -- Ambiguous short name: must never print the OTHER module's constructor.
    let a = A.ADup(1)
    let b = B.BDup("s")
    println("dup_a_not_wrong=" ++ bool_to_string(not(string_contains(to_string(a), "BDup"))))
    println("dup_b_not_wrong=" ++ bool_to_string(not(string_contains(to_string(b), "ADup"))))
  end

  mod A do
    type Dup = ADup(Int)
  end
  mod B do
    type Dup = BDup(String)
  end
end
